course: dictionary
lesson: 12766
title: Earnings: money from work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Earnings are the money a person gets for working. Wages and salary are kinds of earnings. Earnings can also mean the profit a business makes, which is the money it keeps after paying its costs. Even pocket money for doing chores counts as earnings.
explain: «Mia's earnings from babysitting were 15 pounds.» The word earnings tells you the money she got for her work. You can see the clue in the word earn: to earn money is to get money by working.
explain: Earnings is often used in maths. «Sam earns 20 pounds an hour. For 8 hours of work, his earnings are 8 × 20 = 160 pounds.» To find total earnings, multiply the money per hour by the number of hours.
fact: Earnings means the money a person gets for working.
fact: «Earnings» is a plural noun, so it is usually used with a plural verb: «His earnings are high.»
fact: Phrases you may see: «weekly earnings», «total earnings», «earnings per hour», «average earnings».
fact: In business news, «company earnings» means the profit a company makes.
fact: To work out total earnings in maths, multiply the amount earned per hour by the number of hours worked.
exercise: «Mia's earnings from babysitting were 15 pounds.» What does earnings mean here? | The children Mia looked after | A card she was given for helping | *The money Mia got for her work | The hours Mia spent asleep
exercise: «The shop's earnings went up this month.» What do earnings mean here? | *The money the shop made from selling things | The number of people in the shop | The shelves the shop had | The lights and heating in the shop
exercise: Sam earns 20 pounds an hour and works 8 hours. What are his earnings? | 28 pounds | 120 pounds | 12 pounds | *160 pounds
test:
Which word is closest in meaning to earnings? | Holidays | *Wages | Weather | Garden
Which of these is an example of earnings? | A library book you borrowed | The weather on Friday | *Money paid for mowing lawns | A bike you were given as a present
exam: What do «total earnings» mean? | *All the money someone got from work, added together | A list of jobs you could do | The first money you ever earned | The number of hours you spent at work
